# 1Password -> Cloudflare secret manifest.
# Format:  <1Password item>  <Cloudflare secret name>.  One column = same name both sides.
# Only these are managed; anything else on the Worker is left untouched and never deleted.

# Backs the evidence extractor (src/core/extract.ts). Without it evaluate_meetup_topic and
# assess_speaker_readiness decline to answer rather than falling back to pattern matching —
# see the fail-closed note in dispatch.ts. So this key is the difference between two working
# services and two services that politely refuse; it is not optional in production.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY               ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN_ELC             SLACK_BOT_TOKEN_ELC
# unmanaged (Cloudflare-only): MCP_USAGE_SLACK_CHANNEL and A2A_TRADE_SLACK_CHANNEL are channel
# IDs, not credentials. STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is pushed by hand per entity, see CLAUDE.md.
